; ============================================================================
; hledger-x epic 3 playground
;
;   hledger-x add -f test.journal
;
; Things to try are marked [TRY] below. `hledger -f test.journal print` shows
; you what hledger makes of all this, which is the thing hledger-x is trying
; to agree with.
;
; A few [TRY]s want a `.hledger-x.toml`. Copy this file somewhere outside the
; repository first and experiment there — the repository root already has a
; `.hledger-x.toml` that the test suite relies on.
; ============================================================================


; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; payee — declared payees are known-good even with no transactions yet
;
; [TRY] At the description prompt, type `bahn` and press Enter. You get
;       "did you mean Deutsche Bahn?" instead of a silently forked payee.
; [TRY] Type `Hof` and press Tab — completes to a payee that appears in no
;       transaction at all.
; [TRY] With `strict = true` under `[add]`, an undeclared payee asks before
;       it is used — the same question accounts and commodities get.
;
; A description is `payee | note`, split at the first `|`. Only the payee half
; is the transaction's identity.
;
; [TRY] Enter `Deutsche Bahn | ticket to Hamburg`. The payee is declared, so
;       nothing complains however new the note is — and the postings are
;       pre-filled from the 2025-12-19 transaction below, whose note is
;       different. A template keyed on the whole description would never have
;       matched.
; [TRY] Enter `Rewe | big shop`, then `Rewe | small shop`. Both are one payee.
; [TRY] Enter `Bahnhof Kiosk | coffee`. What comes back names the *payee* —
;       `Bahnhof Kiosk` — not the whole string. (A passing note by default; a
;       question if you turned `strict` on.)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
payee Deutsche Bahn
payee Hofpfisterei
payee Rewe
payee Transfer to savings

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; tag — declared tags complete after a `;`
;
; [TRY] At the description prompt type `Rewe ; ` and press Tab: the tag pool
;       appears. `tri` + Tab completes to `trip:`.
; [TRY] Keep going: `Rewe ; trip: berlin, rec` + Tab. Completion resumes after
;       the comma, but is silent inside a tag's value — that is free text.
; [TRY] Comments work on amounts too: `18.20 EUR ; receipt: yes`.
;       `client` below is never declared; it is picked up from the comment on
;       the 2026-08-09 transaction.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tag trip
tag receipt

commodity 1,000.00 EUR

account assets:bank:checking
account assets:bank:savings
account assets:cash
account expenses:bakery
account expenses:groceries
account expenses:travel:train
account liabilities:creditcard


; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Y / year — partial dates below take the declared year
;
; These three transactions used to be skipped with a warning. They are now
; parsed, so they feed completion and the transaction templates.
;
; [TRY] Description `Hofpfisterei` — its template comes from a 01-07 date that
;       only exists because of the `Y 2026` above it.
; [TRY] Note that anything hledger-x *writes* gets a full YYYY-MM-DD date,
;       even here. Explicit beats implicit, and a full date cannot be
;       silently rebound by editing a `Y` line above it.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Y 2025

11-03 Rewe
    expenses:groceries        23.45 EUR
    assets:bank:checking     -23.45 EUR

12-19 Deutsche Bahn | ticket to Hamburg  ; trip: hamburg, receipt: yes
    expenses:travel:train     49.00 EUR
    assets:bank:checking     -49.00 EUR

Y 2026

01-07 Hofpfisterei
    expenses:bakery            4.20 EUR
    assets:cash               -4.20 EUR


; A full date still means exactly what it says.
2026-08-01 Rewe
    expenses:groceries        18.20 EUR
    liabilities:creditcard   -18.20 EUR


; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; alias — `bahn` below is not an account, it is a rewrite of one
;
; [TRY] At an account prompt, type `trav` and Tab. You get
;       `expenses:travel:train` — the account hledger sees — not the bare
;       `bahn` this file spells it with. Before epic 3 the completion pool
;       held the half-name.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
alias bahn=expenses:travel:train

2026-08-02 Deutsche Bahn  ; trip: koeln
    bahn                      31.00 EUR
    assets:bank:checking     -31.00 EUR

end aliases


; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; apply account — everything in here is written as a *remainder*
;
; `savings` on the next transaction is really `assets:bank:savings`. Writing
; the full name in this region would produce
; `assets:bank:assets:bank:savings`, which is the trap epic 3 exists to close.
;
; [TRY] The region is closed, so a plain append never lands in it. To land
;       inside it, put this in a .hledger-x.toml beside your copy:
;
;           [add]
;           insertion = "chronological"
;
;       then enter a transaction dated 2026-08-05 (after the 08-04 below,
;       before the 08-09 further down). Enter the accounts by their full
;       names — `assets:bank:savings`, `assets:bank:checking` — and watch
;       hledger-x write the remainders. `hledger -f test.journal print` will
;       read back exactly the accounts you typed.
; [TRY] With chronological insertion still on, try the same date with
;       `expenses:groceries` and `assets:cash`. Neither can be spelled
;       anywhere in this region, so hledger-x refuses: it names every account
;       it cannot write and the directive and line responsible, leaves the
;       file untouched, and keeps your entry in the recovery journal.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apply account assets:bank

2026-08-04 Transfer to savings
    savings                  100.00 EUR
    checking                -100.00 EUR

end apply account


; Back outside the region: plain full names again. A plain `hledger-x add`
; appends after this, where nothing is in effect.
2026-08-09 Rewe  ; client: acme
    expenses:groceries         9.99 EUR
    assets:cash               -9.99 EUR
